note seed/node/tests/view-prep.om: view-prep ROUND40 BASE ID[,ID...] [WRONG], the DRA-291 view-test
note fixture (nd_prep of nodedrv.om), the Omega port of view-prep.py with byte-identical output.
note ROUND40 holds final-selected.json. BASE is rebuilt with root/ (the broken files), work/,
note objs.txt (one objective argument per line), expect.json and map (fake-serve's format:
note "<klen> <vlen>\n" key value; the key is the prompt as a JSON string, as omnode-infer writes it
note into its request body, the value the completion answer carrying the recorded raw output). Each
note ID selects the first run whose job path contains it. With a fifth argument (WRONG) the first
note objective's goal becomes K+N+A+1, which the map has no turns for and a redirect corrects.
note Prints the objective lines. Exit 0, 1 when the fixture cannot be prepared, 2 for usage.
note Composition: om2, seed/json/json.om, seed/node/tests/drv.om, seed/node/tests/nodedrv.om, this.

text vpusage "usage: view-prep ROUND40 BASE ID[,ID...] [WRONG]\n"
text vperr "view-prep: cannot prepare the fixture\n"

fn main to int
cx = new uchar 65536 0
js = new uchar 983040 0
tp = new uint dvtcap 0
ids = new uchar 4096 0
if lt dv_argc 4
x = dv_err vpusage
ret 2
end
a = dv_arg 1 part cx 8192 4096
b = dv_arg 2 part cx 16384 4096
k = dv_arg 3 ids
if or or lt a 1 lt b 1 lt k 0
x = dv_err vpusage
ret 2
end
put ndl 2 ulong a
put ndl 4 ulong b
r = nd_prep cx js tp view part ids 0 ulong k gt dv_argc 4
if lt r 0
x = dv_err vperr
ret 1
end
x = dv_out view part cx 32768 get ndl 8
ret 0
end
